SUMMARY:Yates Mill Garden Workday (Raleigh)
DESCRIPTION:Join NCWF South Wake Conservationists Chapter for a Pollinator Garden Clean‑Up at Yates Mill County Park! The SWC Gardens & Wildlife Habitats Committee is hosting a garden maintenance event at the native pollinator garden at Yates Mill County Park. We’ll be working in two volunteer shifts—choose the one that fits your comfort level. \nShift 1: 10:00 AM – 11:30 AM – For volunteers experienced or willing to help pull out poison ivy and thorny bramble. Long sleeves and long pants are strongly recommended. \nShift 2: 11:00 AM – 1:00 PM – General garden maintenance: weeding\, thinning\, and tidying. You may encounter poison ivy; we can help you identify it. \nWe look forward to working together to care for this beautiful pollinator garden and support the wildlife that depends on it! \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/yates-mill-garden-workday-raleigh/
CATEGORIES:Featured
END:VEVENT
